  <div class="prose mx-auto">
    <p>After 13 issues, I’m ending The Defender’s Dispatch. Issue 013, published on November 9, will be the last.</p>

    <p>When I started the newsletter in August, I wanted a place to spend more time with the cybersecurity and IT stories that deserved it. Security Signal Weekly covers the stories to watch; the Dispatch gave me room to connect those stories to the work of defending and supporting real systems. I’m glad I made that space.</p>

    <p>Making an issue took more than writing the email. I chose and checked the stories, wrote the web edition, prepared the mailing, checked the links and layout, and made sure the published page was actually there before sending. I also built the signup, confirmation, and reader submission pieces around it. I wanted the whole thing to be useful and reliable. Keeping all of those pieces moving every week became harder than I expected.</p>

    <p>Some issues went out later than planned, including the last one. The weekly deadline became a source of stress, and keeping all of it going began to feel heavier than the writing itself. I don’t want to keep promising another issue when that commitment is wearing on me. So I’m ending the Dispatch here.</p>

    <p>Thank you to everyone who subscribed, read an issue, or sent a story my way. I’m proud of the work in the <a href="/newsletter/archive/">archive</a>, and it will stay available here. I’ll keep writing about cybersecurity and IT on <a href="/blog/">the blog</a>, including Security Signal Weekly.</p>

    <p>Subscribers don’t need to do anything. There won’t be another regular Dispatch issue.</p>

    <p>— Kyle</p>
  </div>
